Hermit: a path crate outside the workspace is first-party.

bootstrap/run-pinned-tool applies this to the pinned Reindeer revision
(bootstrap/tool-pins.sh) before it builds it; the patch's content is part of
the build key. Hermit path-depends on the crates of its reverie submodule and
keeps them out of its workspace. Pinned Reindeer treats such a crate as
third-party and fails ("crate sources would be inaccessible from the generated
BUCK file") because its sources are outside shim/third-party/rust. The reverie
Buck cell builds those crates, so Reindeer must walk them for their
dependencies (crates only Reverie uses need rules too) and emit no rules for
them: what it already does for workspace members. A per-crate omit_targets
fixup is not enough: it stops the walk, and the crates only Reverie uses lose
their rules. Drop this patch once Reindeer offers a way to say so.

The match is wider than its title: Source::Local is every path crate, so a path
crate under shim/third-party/rust would get no rules either. Today every path
crate that is not a workspace member is one of the reverie submodule's 16
crates (Cargo.lock: 38 path packages, 22 workspace members). Vendor a new
third-party crate from a registry or git source, or narrow this match first.

diff --git a/src/buckify.rs b/src/buckify.rs
index 8386185..cd676dc 100644
--- a/src/buckify.rs
+++ b/src/buckify.rs
@@ -298,8 +298,12 @@ fn generate_rules<'scope, 'env>(
         let will_use_rules = {
             let is_private_root_pkg =
                 context.index.is_root_package(pkg) && !context.index.is_public_package(pkg);
+            // Hermit (bootstrap/patches/reindeer): a path dependency outside the
+            // workspace (Source::Local) is first-party too; the Buck cell that
+            // holds it builds it. Walk it for its dependencies, emit nothing.
             let is_ignored_workspace_package = !context.config.include_workspace_members
-                && context.index.is_workspace_package(pkg);
+                && (context.index.is_workspace_package(pkg)
+                    || matches!(pkg.source, Source::Local));
             !is_private_root_pkg && !is_ignored_workspace_package
         };
 
